{"author":{"id":"f943aa1c5ee078b881a8e97535a4e2ccb401d01ca00f4128126befa9cca58a32"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1792675295,"nonce":"YovmU+Ag+hFDLctMw9pjYd11HLk=","target":"c2ede78ada170febff6fbcfb3d814de68762c1001055b4694d7725d05d95ec70","message":"## M6 handover: steps 2 (Risk), 5 (Code), 7 (Verify)\n\nBranch `b768fbb-m6-risk-code-verify` at 6b94027, rebased on main 6a72039 (M4, PR #46). `make ci` passes at 6b94027.\n\n### What's in it\n- **Step 2 (C2), CycleRisk.vue:** the three classes in C2's words, the AI's suggestion, and Set \u003cclass\u003e. The server action `suggest-risk` (internal/ai: one OpenAI-compatible chat call) posts the AI's class as a step-2 comment (meta `ai:risk`, `ai:model`).\n- **Step 5 (C5), CycleCode.vue:** the agent strip, and the commits with a +/- total. The tiles show step 4's tests, the base's checks at the head (M4's gate, signed by whom), and the PR's checks. The PR's title and description can be edited; this adds ghpr `Edit` and `PATCH /api/issues/{id}/pulls/{n}`. Mark ready for review goes through M4's gated POST.\n- **Step 7 (C7), CycleVerify.vue:** who and when for each criterion (\"the merge\" when it was checked at the merge commit), the run tile, plan delivered, \"waits for k of n criteria\", and Sign off \u003cstatus\u003e / Send back.\n- **The run at the merged head, wired to M4:**\n  - `/tests` returns `merged`, which is `proof.Gate` at `pr.merge_commit`.\n  - The run tile reads Pass / Failed / Not run with the signer.\n  - When the base declares checks, the sign-off answers 400 \"not proven at \u003csha\u003e: \u003creason\u003e\", and a reason overrides it.\n  - Test: `TestCycleSignoffNotProvenAtMerge`.\n\n### Rulings\n- The AI's suggestion is a comment, never the risk field. A person sets the class.\n- The AI key comes only from `LLM_API_KEY` in the server's environment. When `LLM_BASE_URL`/`LLM_MODEL` are unset, the address and model fall back to the first provider in `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`. opencode's auth store is never read. With no address, the AI is off and the box is hidden.\n- Board drags and status PATCHes skip the gates (the PRD's floor rule). Only the step's own button gates.\n- `Stages.Roles` was added, so step 2's footer and step 7's bar name the role.\n- Sign off stays disabled in the browser until every criterion is checked. The server keeps only the person rule and the run/proof rule.\n- When the base declares checks, the proof at the merge commit replaces a pasted run, and a reason overrides it. When no checks are declared, a pasted `verify:run` at the merge still counts, as before.\n- A merge commit that isn't fetched yet counts as not proven: `/tests` lists the declared checks as not proven, and the sign-off refuses without a reason. `proof.Gate` only errors when checks are declared.\n\n### Deferred\n- `[ai] model` in the toml (dev-cycle.md's M6), and a Settings › AI page.\n- A \"how\" line on a checked criterion, and per-commit +/- stats (the endpoint only has the total).\n- A server-side criteria gate on sign-off (today it's only in the browser).\n- An \"open the agent\" link from step 5's strip (the Worktrees tab covers it).\n- At 900px the header nav overlaps \"Send\"/\"Inbox\". That's existing nav code, not M6.\n\n### What was seen in the browser\n- Steps 2, 5 and 7 were checked at 1440px and 900px on a clone of guilbep/git-board-test in $TMPDIR.\n- The PR parts (draft PR #30, merged PR #31, the checks, the gate at head and merge) came from routed responses, because the sandbox clone has no git-bug GitHub token. The scratch PRs #30 and #31 and the branch m6-base are left on git-board-test.\n- No real AI call was made: no `LLM_API_KEY` in this session. The client is covered by httptest in internal/ai and by `TestCycleSuggestRisk*`.\n\n### Remaining\n- Nothing for M6. The coordinator rebases and lands.","files":null}]}